  "configuration_id": "config_030",
  "reason": "Evidence: RNA-only with scvi_n200 + multiprofile + avgpool (config_005, acc=0.650) is the best result so far, and image-only with resnet50 is very weak (config_010, acc=0.208). The critical untested question is whether the image modality, despite its poor standalone performance, provides any complementary signal when fused with the strongest RNA representation. This experiment (config_030: multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, resnet50, avgpool, concat) directly tests that question by taking the best RNA-only configuration and adding image via the simplest fusion (concat). It changes only one design axis (adding image + fusion) relative to config_005, isolating the marginal contribution of the image modality. If config_030 does not meaningfully exceed 0.650, it strongly indicates resnet50 features are uninformative here and we should focus remaining budget on RNA-side improvements or a stronger image encoder. If it does exceed, it justifies further exploration of fusion strategies and ViT-based image encoders. This is the highest-information experiment under the limited budget because it resolves the go/no-go decision for the entire multimodal branch."
}

